[2026-02-08] MEASUREMENT: V2 accuracy 36.0% (n=2,411) — barely above random (33.3%). Binomial p=0.002 but Cohen's h=0.059 (negligible). Only 2.45pp above always-neutral baseline.
[2026-02-08] MEASUREMENT: By direction: Bearish 43.3% (n=490), Neutral 37.1% (n=1406), Bullish 26.6% (n=515). Bullish is BELOW random baseline (32.1%).
[2026-02-08] MEASUREMENT: By category: Forex 55.4% (n=466), Indices 34.5%, Crypto 30.9%, Stocks 30.7%, Commodities 30.4%.
[2026-02-08] FINDING: **NO LLM can distinguish bullish from bearish**. Grok scores 0.336 vs 0.305. GPT-5 scores 0.243 vs 0.179 (INVERSE). Perplexity scores 0.283 vs 0.013 (INVERSE). Bullish/bearish signals are noise.
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Forex 55.4% accuracy is ARTIFACT — forex markets are 64.2% neutral, system predicts neutral → matches. Directional forex: bearish 27.5%, bullish 32.8% (both below random).
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Directional calls by ANY LLM are 15-24% accurate (worse than coin flip). Claude 23.7%, GPT-5 21.4%, Grok 19.9%, Perplexity 14.7%.
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Feb 7 "64% accuracy spike" was flat market illusion — neutral predictions 85.4% correct because market was flat. Bearish/bullish that day: 5-12%.
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Bearish crypto is consistently strong: BTC 100% (8/8), BNB 100% (3/3), SOL 69% (9/13), ETH 55% (6/11). Overall bearish crypto: 73.9% (n=65).
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Medium LLM disagreement (0.25-0.40) yields 43.7% accuracy vs 33.9% for low disagreement. Moderate disagreement has signal.
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Confidence does NOT predict accuracy — r=0.12 (1.4% variance explained). High-confidence directional: 25% (worse than low-confidence 44%).
[2026-02-08] FINDING: V3 is worse than V2: 28.5% vs 30.6% head-to-head on 8,079 matched pairs. V3 has higher neutral rate (71.2% vs 61.9%).
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Ensemble does NOT destroy value vs Grok alone: Grok standalone 20.9% (not 53.3% — earlier metric was misleading). Ensemble actually corrects Grok more than it overrides (35.4% vs 14.8%).
[2026-02-08] FINDING: Perplexity 60% failure rate confirmed (2,379 rows vs 5,952 for others). With Perplexity: 38.6% accuracy. Without: 41.6%.
[2026-02-08] FINDING: V3 evaluator IS working (1,498 evaluated), contradicting Feb 4 finding.
[2026-02-08] **DECISION: NO-GO on current prediction algorithms**. 36.0% accuracy is negligible effect size. No LLM can predict direction. System's only "skill" is predicting neutral (= "I don't know").
